                    "id": "obj-1",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 20.0, 15.0, 600.0, 24.0 ],
                    "text": "Teardown hooks: cleaning up after a test"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-2",
                    "linecount": 7,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 20.0, 45.0, 480.0, 100.0 ],
                    "text": "[mUnit.teardown] is the counterpart of [mUnit.loadbang]: it bangs once the handler has frozen this patch's results, after the result files are written and before the patch would be closed or Max quit. Use it to stop what the test started.\n\nThe handler waits for every teardown to report done (up to teardownMs, see munit.config.js) before it goes on. Console errors while teardowns run never fail the suite."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "numinlets": 0,
                    "numoutlets": 1,
                    "outlettype": [ "" ],
                    "patching_rect": [ 693.0, 15.0, 98.5, 22.0 ],
                    "text": "mUnit.harness"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-4",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 2,
                    "outlettype": [ "bang", "bang" ],
                    "patching_rect": [ 693.0, 55.0, 98.5, 22.0 ],
                    "text": "mUnit.handler"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-6",
                    "linecount": 2,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 20.0, 153.0, 416.0, 33.0 ],
                    "text": "1. The test: a metro counts up; the assert passes when the count reaches 3. The metro is still running afterwards."
                }
